@orders = http://localhost:5102
@menu = http://localhost:5101

### Start MenuService and OrderService in separate terminals.
GET {{menu}}/api/menu

### Create a Pending order using IDs from the menu (201)
# @name createOrder
POST {{orders}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Classroom Customer",
  "items": [
    { "menuItemId": 1, "quantity": 2 },
    { "menuItemId": 5, "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### Retrieve the order, including saved name/price snapshots (200)
GET {{orders}}/api/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.orderId}}

### List orders, newest first (200)
GET {{orders}}/api/orders

### Payment is not integrated: Pending -> Paid is blocked (409)
PUT {{orders}}/api/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Paid" }

### Cancel the Pending order (200); repeat is an idempotent no-op
PUT {{orders}}/api/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Cancelled" }

### Invalid quantity (400, no order created)
POST {{orders}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Classroom Customer",
  "items": [{ "menuItemId": 1, "quantity": 0 }]
}

### Missing product (400, no order created)
POST {{orders}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Classroom Customer",
  "items": [{ "menuItemId": 2147483647, "quantity": 1 }]
}

### Stop MenuService, then send this: 503, no order created.
### Restart MenuService and resend: 201. Existing orders remain readable during outage.
POST {{orders}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Dependency Failure Demo",
  "items": [{ "menuItemId": 1, "quantity": 1 }]
}
